 "rationale": "The circuit computes a GF(2^4) product mod x^4+x+1 into zero-init outputs; since q8-q11 are still |0> just before g18 (the intermediate CNOTs act on zeros), T0-T14 become no-ops and T15 writes the full product. It uses 9 two-level Karatsuba ANDs on input parities, each a 4-T Gidney AND into one reused ancilla, then CNOTs into the outputs and a measurement-based uncompute. That gives 36 T and 13 qubits, against the 64 T achieved so far."
